 sector by 9.8 percent all  of this is making investors feel that  most likely the outlook for the second  half of 2019 is again more promising all  right one more question for you  Catherine because I found I heard that  PSA group the French carmaker group the  deliveries in China slumped 60% in the  first half of the year so that is quite  worrying you certainly for some foreign  investors is Beijing going to counter  any of that certainly the slowdown in  terms of what the government's been  doing they've been tweaking policy both  monetary wise and fiscally speaking but  in terms of what the focus should be for  investors for the third quarter fourth  quarter it really is on the fiscal side  of things so further infrastructure  investment not like we saw in 2008 but  more targeted infrastructure investment  and then really encouraging businesses  to again reinvest and doing so by  relaxing measures such as tax cuts etc  so really to aid sentiment versus  overall just boosting growth  all right carefully and young there in  Hong Kong and Daniel Cooper from the  Frankfurt Stock Exchange thank you to  both of you
 

